Perform one final READ-ONLY forensic reconstruction of the completed /work-on
run for homelab-iac #88 / PR #221.

Do not modify the branch, PR, issues, labels, tests, telemetry, or tracker.
Do not propose a fix yet.

The purpose is to explain why this run took more than 3 hours and whether the
cost came from the inherent investigation, validation, proof/evidence
construction, or the /work-on review topology.

Use raw harness/session evidence and Moraine if available. Do not rely only on
the PR telemetry summary.

## 1. Exact candidate/review chain

Reconstruct the complete chronological chain from base
93f69bc8044172900952ceda6bf5552bfc7968a3 to final
d9bc7e59aede459812880772f7dcb94d002aa403.

For every committed candidate, give:

- commit SHA/message;
- what materially changed;
- whether it changed production behavior, test/evidence apparatus, or both;
- which review/checkpoint preceded it;
- which accepted blocker(s) caused it;
- which review gate followed it.

Explicitly identify:
- the first committed candidate C0;
- every Reviewed anchor;
- every Corrective batch;
- every delta gate;
- every fresh cumulative confirmation.

Explain why telemetry contains:
- 12 full reviews = four three-axis cumulative gates;
- 15 delta reviews = five three-axis delta gates.

## 2. Accepted blocker census

There are 10 reported resolved blocking findings.

Enumerate all 10 individually.

For each record:

- discovery stage: readiness / initial cumulative / delta / final cumulative;
- review axis;
- governing acceptance criterion/hard rule;
- concise finding;
- correction commit;
- primary cause using the frozen #107 vocabulary:
  remediation-introduced / remediation-worsened / pre-existing-missed /
  sibling / re-raised / contract-or-surface / delta-miss /
  cumulative-only / nondeterministic-environmental / unknown;
- zero or more secondary tags;
- whether it concerned:
  A. production correctness,
  B. reproduction/harness correctness,
  C. direct-evidence/provenance sufficiency,
  D. repository/testing contract,
  E. other.

For remediation-introduced/worsened, name the earlier directive/commit that
caused it. Do not infer causality merely from adjacency.

## 3. Why so many gates?

For each of the five delta gates and each subsequent cumulative confirmation:

- Did the delta gate find an accepted blocker?
- Did the following cumulative confirmation find an accepted blocker that the
  just-completed delta gate missed?
- If yes, was that later finding legitimately cumulative-only, outside delta
  scope, or a true delta miss under #102?
- Did any cumulative confirmation effectively reread/prove the same unchanged
  material without yielding distinct assurance?

